  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">

      <exercise>
        <problem>
        <para><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_3_6_5_PP"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise><exercise>
          <problem>
          <para><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_3_6_5_PP_a"/></para>
          </problem>
          </exercise><exercise>
            <problem>
            <para><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_3_6_5_PP_b"/></para>
            </problem>
            </exercise><exercise>
              <problem>
              <para><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_3_6_5_PP_c"/></para>
              </problem>
              </exercise>


      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
        <exercise id="e33d6517-71c2-4b13-a3ad-973e596b0bce" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00002">1. Chloe creates a scatter plot showing the relationship between the number of
              steps she takes and her heart rate. The correlation coefficient of the line of best
              fit is 0.88.</para>
            <para id="para-00003">Are they correlated? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
            <para id="para-00004">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00005">Yes, the correlation coefficient is close to 1, so they are correlated.</para>
            <para id="para-00006">No, the correlation coefficient is close to 1.</para>
            <para id="para-00007">Yes, the correlation coefficient is more than 0.</para>
            <para id="para-00008">No, the correlation coefficient is more than 0.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00009">Correct! Yes, the correlation coefficient is close to 1.</para>
            <para id="para-00010">Try again. Revisit activities 3.6.3 – 3.6.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00011">The correct answer is: Yes, the correlation coefficient is close to 1, so they are
              correlated. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_14b0ea10-389e-4c85-b327-d2c875104094" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00012">2. Kiran creates a scatter plot showing the relationship between the number of
              students attending drama club and the number of students attending poetry club each
              week. The correlation coefficient for the line of best fit is –0.36.</para>
            <para id="para-00013">Are they strongly correlated? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
            <para id="para-00014">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00015">Yes, the correlation coefficient is close to 0.</para>
            <para id="para-00016">No, the correlation coefficient is negative.</para>
            <para id="para-00017">Yes, the correlation coefficient is more than 0.</para>
            <para id="para-00018">No, the correlation coefficient is closer to 0.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00019">Correct! No, the correlation coefficient is closer to 0.</para>
            <para id="para-00020">Try again. Revisit activities 3.6.3 – 3.6.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00021">The correct answer is: No, the correlation coefficient is closer to 0. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="f0316244-fc14-42b4-9754-c47a6ba6e6a5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00022">3. Which of the following is a causal relationship?</para>
            <para id="para-00023">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00024">The number of minutes spent running and the number of calories burned.</para>
            <para id="para-00025">The temperature outside and number of people wearing shorts.</para>
            <para id="para-00026">The number of people in a family and the amount of the electric bill.</para>
            <para id="para-00027">The age of a person and the number of words they know.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00028">Correct! The number of minutes spent running and the number of calories burned.</para>
            <para id="para-00029">Try again. Revisit activity 3.6.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00030">The correct answer is: The number of minutes spent running and the number of
              calories burned. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="cdd0d881-4f00-4469-b3fc-879ba7fb46ca" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00031">4. Which of the following is a causal relationship?</para>
            <para id="para-00032">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00033">The number of children in a family and the number of pets in the home.</para>
            <para id="para-00034">The amount of sugar a person eats and their level of happiness.</para>
            <para id="para-00035">The number of students in a school and the state test scores.</para>
            <para id="para-00036">The number of miles driven and the cost of gas.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00037">Correct! The number of miles driven and the cost of gas.</para>
            <para id="para-00038">Try again. Revisit activity 3.6.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00039">The correct answer is: The number of miles driven and the cost of gas. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
